speechtext:
This item is made up as follows :	Printing and stationery, $13,000;
military survey, $4,000-a survey carried on by the pupils of the Royal Military college, under the direction of a competent officer of the college, which has been going on for some years ; injuries at annual drill, covering cases of illness and accidents to men and occasionally to horses, $2,000 ; telegraphic expenses, legal expenses, and sundries, $3,000. It is the usual vote.
Royal Military College, $75,000.
